WEBVTT

1
00:50:40.906 --> 00:50:46.906
I am going to share something from God's Word about giving now as well.

2
00:50:46.906 --> 00:50:56.906
And I actually want to make grateful use of what Bram told us last week about giving.

3
00:50:56.906 --> 00:51:05.906
Because it encouraged me somewhat, as there are a number of people in this church who have a role to say something about giving each time.

4
00:51:05.906 --> 00:51:12.906
And then you sometimes have the feeling that creeps over you, oh yes, do I have to do that again?

5
00:51:12.906 --> 00:51:20.906
It's not pleasant to, especially for Belgians, because I am a Belgian, even though I have been told I have a Dutch accent from time to time.

6
00:51:20.906 --> 00:51:24.906
Okay. Okay.

7
00:51:25.906 --> 00:51:31.906
Is that so? Now I am a bit lost in my thread.

8
00:51:31.906 --> 00:51:36.906
But I actually want to continue on what Bram told us last week.

9
00:51:36.906 --> 00:51:41.906
And a Belgian doesn't like to talk about finances. That's just in us.

10
00:51:41.906 --> 00:51:45.906
We are the kind of people who feel like, just leave us alone.

11
00:51:45.906 --> 00:51:48.906
It's already strange enough.

12
00:51:49.906 --> 00:52:00.906
So indeed, as a Belgian, I was encouraged to say, look at what Bram said about making.

13
00:52:00.906 --> 00:52:06.906
And we will even read that in 2 Corinthians 9 verse 7. Maybe I can read it first, because that makes it a bit more logical.

14
00:52:06.906 --> 00:52:13.906
So I passed it on, everyone must decide for themselves how much they want to give.

15
00:52:14.906 --> 00:52:18.906
And then you see the word decide there.

16
00:52:18.906 --> 00:52:21.906
And that is what Bram encouraged us about last week.

17
00:52:21.906 --> 00:52:28.906
You need to think about it and you need to make the decision to give.

18
00:52:28.906 --> 00:52:41.906
And God is not so much concerned about the fact that you immediately, and it is also advice that Bram gave, go to that 10%, but you need to start on the way there.

19
00:52:42.906 --> 00:52:51.906
I need to think back, also in the Bible it says in various places that God is not really interested in our offerings.

20
00:52:51.906 --> 00:52:55.906
He is primarily interested in your heart.

21
00:52:55.906 --> 00:53:02.906
And what we do here with giving, and financial giving, is something that must come from a heart that you have for God.

22
00:53:02.906 --> 00:53:05.906
Because otherwise it becomes impossible to do this.

23
00:53:05.906 --> 00:53:08.906
And the intention is to work towards that.

24
00:53:09.906 --> 00:53:13.906
So make that decision. That is what is stated here.

25
00:53:13.906 --> 00:53:17.906
Everyone must decide for themselves how much they want to give.

26
00:53:17.906 --> 00:53:22.906
That means if you are married, you do that together with your wife.

27
00:53:24.906 --> 00:53:31.906
Regardless of the fact that you as a man might bring in 90% of the income, and your wife 10%, it doesn't matter.

28
00:53:33.906 --> 00:53:34.906
You are one.

29
00:53:34.906 --> 00:53:40.906
You decide together what you do with the 10% that you want to give to God.

30
00:53:40.906 --> 00:53:44.906
If you find it necessary, discuss it with your whole family.

31
00:53:45.906 --> 00:53:47.906
Because your children can also learn something from that.

32
00:53:48.906 --> 00:53:52.906
Decide how much you want to give.

33
00:53:52.906 --> 00:53:58.906
Another piece, which I actually took from last week, was actually something like...

34
00:53:59.906 --> 00:54:06.906
...that you should not be mistaken in the fact that if you give 10%, then you are okay with God.

35
00:54:06.906 --> 00:54:08.906
And let me explain that for a moment.

36
00:54:08.906 --> 00:54:12.906
You can, for example, earn money in a wrong way.

37
00:54:13.906 --> 00:54:19.906
And think, if I give 10% of that to God, God has blessed that.

38
00:54:19.906 --> 00:54:21.906
That is also not what is stated here.

39
00:54:21.906 --> 00:54:24.906
That is not what God is going to do, I can really impress that upon you.

40
00:54:24.906 --> 00:54:32.906
God is not going to bless you if you use your money in a wrong way or earn it as income.

41
00:54:32.906 --> 00:54:33.906
He is not going to do that.

42
00:54:34.906 --> 00:54:37.906
Then you may give 50%, he will not bless it.

43
00:54:39.906 --> 00:54:41.906
So decide how much you want to give.

44
00:54:41.906 --> 00:54:48.906
And let it be, if you do that, it must also be done wholeheartedly, without reluctance, without coercion.

45
00:54:48.906 --> 00:54:52.906
And God loves people who give with a cheerful heart.

46
00:54:52.906 --> 00:54:55.906
Isn't that beautiful? Who doesn't want God to love him?

47
00:54:56.906 --> 00:55:00.906
If you give with a cheerful heart, God will love you.

48
00:55:00.906 --> 00:55:04.906
He already loves you, but you could say He loves you even more.

49
00:55:04.906 --> 00:55:07.906
It's difficult to explain, I also have too little time to explain that now.

50
00:55:07.906 --> 00:55:12.906
And God is able to give you everything abundantly.

51
00:55:12.906 --> 00:55:16.906
As a result, you will have more than enough in all things at all times.

52
00:55:16.906 --> 00:55:17.906
That is a promise from God.

53
00:55:17.906 --> 00:55:21.906
And as a result, you can also give to others.

54
00:55:21.906 --> 00:55:25.906
The fact that you give, and that you might receive that back,

55
00:55:25.906 --> 00:55:29.906
is not meant for you to think, that's a nice investment.

56
00:55:29.906 --> 00:55:32.906
That is not what God wants to achieve with this.

57
00:55:32.906 --> 00:55:37.906
That you say, you are a businessman, or you have some investments, or you do that in your free time.

58
00:55:37.906 --> 00:55:41.906
Ah yes, that's a good investment, if I give 10%, then I get 100% back.

59
00:55:41.906 --> 00:55:43.906
That is not the intention.

60
00:55:43.906 --> 00:55:45.906
It is not an investment plan.

61
00:55:46.906 --> 00:55:48.906
Giving to God is not an investment plan.

62
00:55:48.906 --> 00:55:54.906
Giving to God ensures that you receive back and can give again.

63
00:55:54.906 --> 00:55:57.906
And do you know what else is stated in verses 10 and 11?

64
00:55:59.906 --> 00:56:01.906
And that is important to realize.

65
00:56:02.906 --> 00:56:07.906
It is also not the case that when we give, and we can give to others,

66
00:56:07.906 --> 00:56:10.906
it is important to brag about it.

67
00:56:10.906 --> 00:56:12.906
Look at how I can.

68
00:56:12.906 --> 00:56:15.906
Look at how many people I help.

69
00:56:15.906 --> 00:56:17.906
Look at what happens with my money.

70
00:56:17.906 --> 00:56:19.906
Look at where you do that.

71
00:56:19.906 --> 00:56:22.906
Here it says, God gives seed to the sower to sow.

72
00:56:22.906 --> 00:56:23.906
He gives it.

73
00:56:23.906 --> 00:56:25.906
No one else, but also bread to eat.

74
00:56:25.906 --> 00:56:27.906
So he provides.

75
00:56:27.906 --> 00:56:32.906
Just as he gives seed to you, he will give you even more seed.

76
00:56:32.906 --> 00:56:35.906
It comes from him people, don't make an illusion about it.

77
00:56:35.906 --> 00:56:43.906
He will ensure that a great harvest will come from your good deeds.

78
00:56:44.906 --> 00:56:47.906
So you will always have plenty.

79
00:56:48.906 --> 00:56:52.906
Why? To be able to give much away.

80
00:56:53.906 --> 00:56:56.906
And there, people will praise God.

81
00:56:56.906 --> 00:56:57.906
He does it.

82
00:56:57.906 --> 00:57:01.906
The intention is that he is honored by this, not myself.

83
00:57:02.906 --> 00:57:07.906
So I want to encourage you to decide to become givers.

84
00:57:08.906 --> 00:57:09.906
Consult with one another.

85
00:57:09.906 --> 00:57:13.906
I have written a prayer that I want to express,

86
00:57:13.906 --> 00:57:15.906
to truly develop that in us.

87
00:57:15.906 --> 00:57:17.906
That attitude of giving.

88
00:57:18.906 --> 00:57:20.906
Maybe we can stand.

89
00:57:26.906 --> 00:57:31.906
Dear Father, we come to you today with gratitude

90
00:57:31.906 --> 00:57:38.906
for all the gifts and promises that you are already abundantly showing us in our lives.

91
00:57:39.906 --> 00:57:42.906
Lord, so often our hearts are filled with worries

92
00:57:42.906 --> 00:57:45.906
and we notice that we focus on our own needs

93
00:57:45.906 --> 00:57:50.906
instead of on you as the one who provides for everything.

94
00:57:51.906 --> 00:57:54.906
Forgive us this lack of trust in you,

95
00:57:54.906 --> 00:57:59.906
for we know that you have promised to provide for all our needs.

96
00:57:59.906 --> 00:58:03.906
According to your riches in glory.

97
00:58:03.906 --> 00:58:06.906
Lord, we want to give all our worries to you

98
00:58:06.906 --> 00:58:09.906
and develop a generous and giving character

99
00:58:09.906 --> 00:58:12.906
that keeps our eyes focused on Jesus.

100
00:58:12.906 --> 00:58:17.906
Instead of worrying and relying on our own insights,

101
00:58:17.906 --> 00:58:19.906
we trust in you.

102
00:58:19.906 --> 00:58:22.906
Lord, we know that we cannot change ourselves,

103
00:58:22.906 --> 00:58:25.906
but we know that through the power of the Holy Spirit

104
00:58:25.906 --> 00:58:28.906
we can take our worries and fears captive

105
00:58:28.906 --> 00:58:30.906
and surrender them to you.

106
00:58:30.906 --> 00:58:35.906
We proclaim your provision over our lives.

107
00:58:35.906 --> 00:58:39.906
You provide for what you say we need.

108
00:58:39.906 --> 00:58:42.906
And that was actually the last thing I wrote down there.

109
00:58:42.906 --> 00:58:45.906
That was really something that was on my heart.

110
00:58:45.906 --> 00:58:48.906
We actually do not know what is good for us,

111
00:58:48.906 --> 00:58:49.906
but God does.

112
00:58:49.906 --> 00:58:53.906
Therefore you provide for what you say we need.

113
00:58:53.906 --> 00:58:56.906
Thank you, in Jesus' name. Amen.

114
00:58:56.906 --> 00:58:57.906
Amen.

115
00:59:03.906 --> 00:59:06.906
Before you sit down, shake hands with each other.

116
00:59:06.906 --> 00:59:08.906
Just act normal.

117
00:59:11.906 --> 00:59:14.906
We are not going to shake hands. Shake hands, man.

118
00:59:14.906 --> 00:59:16.906
Give a hug, give a kiss.

119
00:59:16.906 --> 00:59:19.906
Or have we just done that? Have we done that already?

120
00:59:19.906 --> 00:59:20.906
Yes, well then.

121
00:59:20.906 --> 00:59:22.906
Just give each other a handshake, man.

122
00:59:26.906 --> 00:59:27.906
Hallelujah.

123
00:59:27.906 --> 00:59:29.906
We are going to start with the Word.

124
00:59:30.906 --> 00:59:32.906
Do you all have your Bible with you?

125
00:59:32.906 --> 00:59:34.906
Show it to me.

126
00:59:39.906 --> 00:59:41.906
Well, that's fine.

127
00:59:41.906 --> 00:59:42.906
Yes, that's fine.

128
00:59:42.906 --> 00:59:43.906
Looks good.

129
00:59:44.906 --> 00:59:50.906
Are there any visitors from Young present?

130
00:59:56.906 --> 01:00:01.906
Let us! Let us! Let us! Let us!

131
01:00:05.906 --> 01:00:06.906
Very nice.

132
01:00:07.906 --> 01:00:08.906
Just very nice for you all.

133
01:00:08.906 --> 01:00:10.906
Everyone just sit down.

134
01:00:13.906 --> 01:00:14.906
Super fun.

135
01:00:15.906 --> 01:00:16.906
Love them.

136
01:00:17.906 --> 01:00:18.906
Hallelujah.

137
01:00:22.906 --> 01:00:25.906
Dear Father in heaven, I thank you for your church.

138
01:00:25.906 --> 01:00:29.906
Lord, I thank you, Jesus, that you are at the head of your church.

139
01:00:29.906 --> 01:00:32.906
And you are a good God. You are our good Lord.

140
01:00:32.906 --> 01:00:34.906
We love you, Jesus.

141
01:00:34.906 --> 01:00:38.906
Lord, I just want to collectively say, we love you, Jesus.

142
01:00:38.906 --> 01:00:40.906
We praise your holy name.

143
01:00:40.906 --> 01:00:44.906
And you are indeed the center of our lives.

144
01:00:44.906 --> 01:00:45.906
And we want to honor you.

145
01:00:45.906 --> 01:00:50.906
And I want to ask you, Holy Spirit, to sow the Word of God, which we are about to discuss,

146
01:00:50.906 --> 01:00:54.906
into the hearts of all the people in this room.

147
01:00:54.906 --> 01:01:00.906
Lord, so that the Word of God is not only heard, but that we can also put it into action

148
01:01:00.906 --> 01:01:03.906
for the transformation of our lives, in Jesus' name.

149
01:01:03.906 --> 01:01:05.906
And we all say amen.

150
01:01:05.906 --> 01:01:06.906
Amen and amen.

151
01:01:07.906 --> 01:01:11.906
It's cute to see that Marco doesn't dare to walk during that prayer.

152
01:01:14.906 --> 01:01:15.906
Amen.

153
01:01:18.906 --> 01:01:21.906
Thank you. But it's good, because the prayer is a holy moment.

154
01:01:21.906 --> 01:01:22.906
Hallelujah.

155
01:01:24.906 --> 01:01:28.906
Have you all happened to read some preparatory work?

156
01:01:28.906 --> 01:01:29.906
Yes, right?

157
01:01:30.906 --> 01:01:31.906
Ezra 2.

158
01:01:32.906 --> 01:01:34.906
We're just going to briefly talk about that.

159
01:01:34.906 --> 01:01:40.906
And I have intentionally asked as homework for all of us to read Ezra 2 ourselves.

160
01:01:40.906 --> 01:01:45.906
That saves me the trouble of having to read all those strange Middle Eastern names.

161
01:01:45.906 --> 01:01:50.906
And then everyone says, that's really not strange, I would say it like that, I would say it like that.

162
01:01:50.906 --> 01:01:55.906
Try it as a pastor to say 300 words, names from that time, here for a moment.

163
01:01:55.906 --> 01:01:58.906
And then they say, no Tim, you have to say it like this, you have to say it like that.

164
01:01:58.906 --> 01:02:00.906
A bunch of know-it-alls, all of you.

165
01:02:01.906 --> 01:02:02.906
Hallelujah.

166
01:02:02.906 --> 01:02:03.906
Praise the name of Jesus.

167
01:02:04.906 --> 01:02:09.906
One of the things, dear church, that we need to learn when we read the Bible,

168
01:02:09.906 --> 01:02:16.906
is that we recognize the genre in which a particular book is written.

169
01:02:16.906 --> 01:02:23.906
The Bible is written as a collection of books, that's why it's called Bible,

170
01:02:23.906 --> 01:02:26.906
that's why it's also called Biblios, that's why it's also called library.

171
01:02:26.906 --> 01:02:36.906
And all those books that are written, they are written by authors with a certain purpose in mind.

172
01:02:36.906 --> 01:02:40.906
Why do they write what they wrote in that time and the reason?

173
01:02:40.906 --> 01:02:43.906
What do they actually want to achieve?

174
01:02:43.906 --> 01:02:47.906
And one of the things we need to understand when we study the Bible,

175
01:02:47.906 --> 01:02:52.906
is that we notice in which genre something is written.

176
01:02:52.906 --> 01:02:58.906
The Bible has quite a few different genres and it is important for us Christians

177
01:02:58.906 --> 01:03:02.906
that we know what we are reading when we are reading something.

178
01:03:02.906 --> 01:03:06.906
Because if you make a mistake, namely, then you will make interpretive errors

179
01:03:06.906 --> 01:03:08.906
and that can sometimes lead to twists.

180
01:03:08.906 --> 01:03:13.906
The genres of the Bible are, for example, law, we have the law.

181
01:03:13.906 --> 01:03:21.906
Poetry, so when David writes something very beautiful about God, then that is poetry.

182
01:03:21.906 --> 01:03:24.906
We have wisdom literature, we have prophecy.

183
01:03:24.906 --> 01:03:28.906
We even have within that prophecy a word called apocalyptic.

184
01:03:28.906 --> 01:03:35.906
That is when God gives revelations of things that are not earthly

185
01:03:35.906 --> 01:03:38.906
and then you get apocalyptic literature.

186
01:03:38.906 --> 01:03:41.906
For example, Ezekiel deals with that.

187
01:03:41.906 --> 01:03:44.906
Daniel describes a lot of apocalyptic.

188
01:03:44.906 --> 01:03:52.906
The book of Revelation, and then these prophets receive insights into things that are not earthly.

189
01:03:52.906 --> 01:03:53.906
That is apocalyptic.

190
01:03:53.906 --> 01:03:57.906
Then of course you have the gospels, which is a genre in itself.

191
01:03:57.906 --> 01:03:59.906
What does gospel mean?

192
01:03:59.906 --> 01:04:01.906
Good news.

193
01:04:01.906 --> 01:04:06.906
And the good news to the people in our world is not that they must come to repentance.

194
01:04:06.906 --> 01:04:09.906
The good news is that Jesus Christ is here.

195
01:04:09.906 --> 01:04:11.906
That is good news.

196
01:04:11.906 --> 01:04:17.906
And that we must come to repentance is a response to the good news that Jesus Christ is here.

197
01:04:17.906 --> 01:04:19.906
Then we have the letters.

198
01:04:19.906 --> 01:04:21.906
Those letters are important.

199
01:04:21.906 --> 01:04:23.906
I think it's so great that we have found them.

200
01:04:23.906 --> 01:04:28.906
That we have our Bible, because it contains so much powerful information.

201
01:04:28.906 --> 01:04:32.906
for the building of the body of Christ, for the building of the family,

202
01:04:32.906 --> 01:04:35.906
of how we can live out our faith for the Lord.

203
01:04:35.906 --> 01:04:37.906
Great that we have that.

204
01:04:37.906 --> 01:04:40.906
And then there is also a genre called narrative.

205
01:04:40.906 --> 01:04:46.906
Narrative is a genre that we can read about in the Bible.

206
01:04:46.906 --> 01:04:51.906
And Ezra and Nehemiah is a narrative genre.

207
01:04:51.906 --> 01:04:55.906
And it is important that we keep a close eye on these genres

208
01:04:55.906 --> 01:04:58.906
and that we know what we are reading,

209
01:04:58.906 --> 01:05:03.906
so that if you were to make a mistake, you would impose something on the Bible

210
01:05:03.906 --> 01:05:06.906
that perhaps should not be at that moment.

211
01:05:06.906 --> 01:05:09.906
Do you all still understand a bit of what I am saying?

212
01:05:09.906 --> 01:05:11.906
I will give you an example.

213
01:05:11.906 --> 01:05:14.906
If David, I say this often, so maybe you have heard this before,

214
01:05:14.906 --> 01:05:16.906
that you think, well, this is repetitive.

215
01:05:16.906 --> 01:05:21.906
But when David says, Lord, you are a rock on which I build,

216
01:05:21.906 --> 01:05:24.906
then that is meant poetically.

217
01:05:24.906 --> 01:05:29.906
So when we would approach David with a Western mindset

218
01:05:29.906 --> 01:05:33.906
and would say, is God a rock? Is God made of stone?

219
01:05:33.906 --> 01:05:38.906
Then David would say, no, that is not what I meant.

220
01:05:38.906 --> 01:05:41.906
That is meant poetically.

221
01:05:41.906 --> 01:05:45.906
And for us Western Christians, it can sometimes be quite a challenge

222
01:05:45.906 --> 01:05:51.906
to approach the Bible, because we, as we have been trained in our schools

223
01:05:51.906 --> 01:05:54.906
and in our society, we are all trained

224
01:05:54.906 --> 01:05:57.906
to try to approach everything factually.

225
01:05:57.906 --> 01:06:00.906
If it says so, then it must be so.

226
01:06:00.906 --> 01:06:02.906
But that is not always true.

227
01:06:02.906 --> 01:06:06.906
For example, when you look at poetry,

228
01:06:06.906 --> 01:06:13.906
poetic things are written to present something beautiful.

229
01:06:13.906 --> 01:06:16.906
And then it is, and that is a very difficult one for us,

230
01:06:16.906 --> 01:06:19.906
it is not meant to be true.

231
01:06:19.906 --> 01:06:22.906
But it is true. Right?

232
01:06:22.906 --> 01:06:27.906
It is the same, for example, with the wisdom literature of King Solomon.

233
01:06:27.906 --> 01:06:32.906
Wisdom is often deep. It is often philosophical.

234
01:06:32.906 --> 01:06:34.906
And sometimes, here we have a very difficult one,

235
01:06:34.906 --> 01:06:39.906
many people in the audience think that, for example, the book of Job is narrative.

236
01:06:39.906 --> 01:06:42.906
But the book of Job is wisdom literature.

237
01:06:42.906 --> 01:06:45.906
So that means, the question is,

238
01:06:45.906 --> 01:06:50.906
is Job really a man who ever existed historically?

239
01:06:50.906 --> 01:06:53.906
And everyone is like, what now? Are you saying Job doesn't exist?

240
01:06:53.906 --> 01:06:56.906


241
01:06:56.906 --> 01:07:01.906
It is not necessarily the intention that we are obligated to take from the Bible

242
01:07:01.906 --> 01:07:03.906
that Job actually existed.

